1
00:00:00,685 --> 00:00:04,185
(Leonard:)for innocent little boys
who just want to be happy?

2
00:00:04,188 --> 00:00:05,618
(Dr Gallo:)Well, I didn't want to say it...

3
00:00:05,623 --> 00:00:07,093
(Leonard:)No, no, say it. Sing it.

4
00:00:07,091 --> 00:00:10,121
(Leonard:)Rent a plane,
write it in the sky.

5
00:00:10,127 --> 00:00:11,597
(Dr Gallo:)Sounds like you're holding on

6
00:00:11,596 --> 00:00:14,126
(Dr Gallo:)to quite a bit of anger
towards her.

7
00:00:14,131 --> 00:00:15,161
(Penny:)Oh, no,
I-I've worked through

8
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:16,566
a lot of that stuff;
I'm better now.

9
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:17,597
(Dr Gallo:)Mm. Good for you.

10
00:00:17,602 --> 00:00:19,032
(Leonard:)Do you know she never let me

11
00:00:19,036 --> 00:00:20,736
(Leonard:)celebrate my birthday
because being born

12
00:00:20,738 --> 00:00:23,738
(Leonard:)was her achievement, not mine?

13
00:00:23,741 --> 00:00:24,971
(Dr Gallo:)That's heartbreaking.

14
00:00:24,976 --> 00:00:28,276
(Leonard:)Right? To this day,
I send her a card every year

15
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,879
(Leonard:)with a little money in it.

16
00:00:32,049 --> 00:00:35,389
(Howard:)You know, once we get
the house back to ourselves,

17
00:00:35,386 --> 00:00:38,386
(Howard:)we can be romantic
in any room we want.

18
00:00:38,389 --> 00:00:41,689
(Bernadette:)Great. I can finally show you
where the laundry room is.

19
00:00:43,561 --> 00:00:45,491
(Stuart:)Boy, who
would've thought

20
00:00:45,496 --> 00:00:48,226
(Stuart:)when you asked me to move in
and help take care of your mom,

21
00:00:48,232 --> 00:00:49,732
(Stuart:)I'd still be here
two years later?

22
00:00:49,734 --> 00:00:52,604
(Bernadette:)Nobody thought that.
No one.

23
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,501
(Stuart:)Well, that's it.

24
00:00:55,506 --> 00:00:57,136
(Bernadette:)I guess so.

25
00:00:58,843 --> 00:01:01,213
(Stuart:)This is weird.
(chuckles)

